  "text": "\n     Voting Information | City of Portsmouth \n      Skip to main content\n\t\t\t\t\t Announcement :   \n\t\t\t\t\t\tFor the November 3, 2026 General Election: Ward 4 Voters will vote at the Portsmouth High School, 50 Andrew Jarvis Drive.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t City of  PORTSMOUTH  NH \n\t\t\t\t\t\t City Clerk \n\t\t\t\t A \n\t\t\t\t A \n\t\t\t\t A \n                \t\t\t\t\t City Clerk \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t Menu \n           Boards \n             Back Copy \n             Created with Sketch. \n         Elected City Officials \n         Boards, Commissions & Committees \n         Vacancies \n         Volunteer Information & Application \n         Meeting Calendar \n           Elections \n             Back Copy \n             Created with Sketch. \n         Elected City Officials \n         Election Results \n         State & National Officials \n         Voting Information \n         Municipal Election Information \n           Ordinances \n             Back Copy \n             Created with Sketch. \n         City Ordinances \n         Noise Control Ordinance \n         Amusement Games Ordinance \n         Bowling Billiards Ordinance \n         Dog License Ordinance \n         Petroleum Products Ordinance \n           Licenses & Permits \n             Back Copy \n             Created with Sketch. \n         List of all Licenses and Permits \n         Birth, Marriage, Divorce & Death \n         Dog License \n         Taxi Licenses  \n         Vendor’s License \n         Events/Parades \n         Sidewalk Performers \n         Amusement Application \n         Bowling/Billiards Application \n         Business License \n         Employment Agencies \n         Pawn Brokers \n         Raffle/Tag Day \n         Sidewalk Obstruction \n           Resources \n             Back Copy \n             Created with Sketch. \n         City Charter \n         Directions to City Hall  \n         Municipal Meetings \n         Reserving City Rooms for Meetings \n         Taxi Business Information \n         Event Organization \n         City Council Revised Orders \n         City Council Policies \nCity of Portsmouth \n                           City Clerk's Office \n                          Voting Information\n Voting Information \n2026 Election \nPrimary \nTuesday, September 8 \nPolling Hours: 8 am-7 pm \nNotices \nCounting of Ballots \nTesting of Ballot Machines \nGeneral Election \nTuesday, November 3 \nPolling Hours: 8 am-7 pm \nNotices \nAbsentee ballot processing starts in each ward at 10:00 am \nJump to \nSample Ballots   Election Forms   Same-Day Registration   How to Register   Which Ward Am I In?   Voting Locations   Board of Registrars   State Districts \nSample Ballots \n(All wards are in each file) \nPDF   2026 General Election Sample Ballots   \nElection Forms \nPDF   2026 Absentee Ballot Application   PDF   Election Worker Interest Form   \nSame Day Voter Registration \nNew voters may register to vote on Election Day at their designated polling location. \nHow and Where to Register to Vote \nYou can register to vote in local, state, and federal elections in New Hampshire if you are: \nA United States citizen \nAt least 18 years old on election day \nA resident in the town/city ward you seek to register in. There is no minimum period you are required to have lived in your community before registering \nTo register to vote, you will be required to complete a Voter Registration Form provided by the Clerk's office or supervisor of the checklist. You will also need to provide proof of your identity, age, U.S. citizenship and domicile (primary residence address). For information on requirements and acceptable documents, see the NH Secretary of State's  voter webpage . \nAm I Registered? \nVisit the Secretary of State's  Voter Information Lookup  page. \nWhich Ward Do I Live In? \nPlease be sure that your address is accurately listed on the checklist to avoid any issues on Election Day. Remember, you must vote in the ward where you reside. \nPDF   Street List by Ward   PDF   Voting Ward Map   PDF   List of Elected Ward Officials   \nQuestions?  Please contact the City Clerk's Office at  (603) 610-7245  or via e-mail at  cityclerk@portsmouthnh.gov . \nVoting Locations by Ward \n1   New Franklin School \n1 Franklin Drive \nOff Woodbury Avenue, between Anchorage Inn and Howard Johnson Hotel \n2   Portsmouth Middle School \n155 Parrott Avenue \nConnie Bean Gymnasium Entrance  \n3   Portsmouth Senior Activity Center \n125 Cottage Street \n4   Portsmouth High School \n50 Andrew Jarvis Drive \n5   Little Harbour School \n50 Clough Drive \nOff of South Street \nBoard of Registrars \nRole Ward Name Email \nRegistrar - Chair At-Large Barbara Ward 16bward1224@gmail.com \nRegistrar 1 Penny Reynolds preynolds21@comcast.net \nWard Two 2 Candace Thayer cshawt@hotmail.com \nWard Three 3 Angelynne Hinson e.hinson@comcast.net \nWard Four 4 Marcia Main marciamain0924@gmail.com \nWard Five 5 Kathleen Boduch kmboduch@portsmouthnh.gov \nRegistrar Assistant 4 Arthur Parrott akparrott@comcast.net \n Registrars Office Number 603-610-7208 \n See a list of all  Election Officials \nState Senate and State Representative Districts \nState Senate District — effective June 1, 2022 \nDistrict 21: New Castle, Newfields, Newington, Newmarket, and Portsmouth \nState Representative Districts — effective June 1, 2022 \nDistrict 21 - Consists of Portsmouth Ward 1 and Newington only \nDistrict 22 - Consists of Portsmouth Ward 5 and New Castle only \nDistrict 26 - Consists of Portsmouth Ward 3 only \nDistrict 27 - Consists of Portsmouth Ward 4 only \nDistrict 28 - Consists of Portsmouth Ward 2 only \nDistrict 37 - Consists of Portsmouth Wards 1 and 5, New Castle and Newington \nDistrict 39 - Floterial with Portsmouth Wards 2, 3 and 4 \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tCity of\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t PORTSMOUTH \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tHome >\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tCity Clerk\nOffice \n1 Junkins Avenue, Portsmouth, NH 03801 \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tHours\nMonday 8 AM – 6 PM \nTuesday 8 AM – 4:30 PM \nWednesday 9 AM – 4:30 PM \nThursday 8 AM – 4:30 PM \nFriday 8 AM – 1 PM \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tPhone\n(603) 610-7245 \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFax\n(603) 610-4158 \nResources \n         Dog Licenses \n         Vital Records \n         Voting Information \n\t\t\t\t\t\t© 2026 - City of Portsmouth. All Rights Reserved. \n                          | \n              \t\t\t                   Terms of Use | Disclaimer                           \t\t\t\t\t \n ",
